Those of you who are interested in reorganizing rec.games.hack to only
cover the game "hack" and in adding a group called rec.games.nethack
for the rest of us should:

  1.  Subscribe to news.groups.announce  (moderated)
  2.  Subscribe to news.groups           (unmoderated)

According to my interpretation of the rules for USENet newsgroup adds,
deletions, reorganizations, renamings, you must take the following
steps.  They publish rules about once a month, and, so, this is from
my fading memory, as I don't have a copy handy:

  1.  Send a "Request for Discussion" (RFD) article to n.g.a which is
      cross-posted to interested or possibly interested newsgroups.
      The RFD must also be cross-posted to n.g, and a "Follow-up to"
      must point to n.g.  All discussion of the proposal must take
      place there.  That is, the powers-that-be want to follow the
      discussion, do so in news.groups, and don't have to subscribe
      to a myriad of groups to follow the discussion.

   2. After a suitable discussion period (months, weeks, I can't recall)
      a "Call for Votes"  (CFV) article is posted.  Votes are sent
      to someone who has to log and count them, and send back a confirmation
      e-mail to each voter.  The CFV has the same cross-postings as the
      RFD.  There may be more than one CFV sent, as a reminder.

   3. At the end of the voting period, the vote counter publishes the
      results, as well as a complete list of Yes, No, and Abstain
      voters.  No secret ballots here.

   4. There has to be a minumim number of votes, and the Yes has to win
      by a large majority.  I can't remember the exact numbers.

   5. The powers-that-be send out newsgroup configuration stuff after
      a positive vote completes.

Now, if you hack players are seriously interested in making changes to
r.g.h, you should take your interest and turn it into an RFD and a CFV.
Also, you'll be taking this discussion to news.groups, which is where
it rightfully belongs!  Then, until your proposed changes take place,
that will leave r.g.h for discussions of the games Nethack and Hack, and
keep the name change and newsgroup metadiscussion elsewhere.

Thank you for your attention.  Now, back to our regular program of
stupid death tricks, interesting spoilers, and requests from people who
never seem to see the FAQ articles.
